# 22. Final Demonstration Scenario

The final project should demonstrate a complete attack-to-response workflow.

### Step 1 — Generate test events

Simulate several failed SSH login attempts.

```text
Failed login
Failed login
Failed login
Failed login
Failed login
```

### Step 2 — Collector

```text
Linux Log
    ↓
Collector
```

### Step 3 — Parser

```text
Raw Log
    ↓
Structured Event
```

### Step 4 — SIEM

The detection engine identifies:

```text
AUTH-001
Possible SSH Brute Force
Severity: HIGH
```

### Step 5 — Alert

The dashboard displays:

```text
HIGH
SSH Brute Force
Source: 192.168.1.50
Status: NEW
```

### Step 6 — SOAR

The corresponding playbook is triggered.

```text
Create Incident
      ↓
Record IP
      ↓
Threat Intelligence Check
      ↓
Request Approval
```

### Step 7 — Response

After approval:

```text
Simulated IP Block
      ↓
Notification
      ↓
Audit Log
```

### Step 8 — Dashboard

The analyst sees:

```text
Incident: INC-001
Status: RESOLVED
Response: IP Blocked
Playbook: SSH Brute Force Response
```

This gives us a complete end-to-end demonstration.

